        "thinking": "Now I understand the routing structure:\n- Most routes are mounted with `api.use(routeFactory(db))` - no prefix\n- Routes inside these factories use absolute paths (e.g., `/companies/:companyId/goals`)\n- The exception: `api.use(\"/companies\", companyRoutes(db))` - the factory uses relative paths (e.g., `/:companyId`, `/`)\n- The api router itself is mounted at `/api` in the app\n\nSo for the CF Worker, we need to handle:\n1. Most route factories: routes are absolute, mounted directly on the app\n\n\n2. `companyRoutes`: routes are relative, mounted under `/companies`\n3. The app is mounted at `/api`\n\nI'll need to tag `expressHandler` wrappers with a marker, walk the Express Router stack to extract route definitions while accounting for the prefix structure, then mount everything on Hono under `/api`. For auth, I'll port the middleware logic directly. Given the complexity, I should parallelize this work with specialized agents handling different parts of the implementation.\n\nActually, let me consolidate this into a single focused agent to build the complete CF infrastructure end-to-end, since the pieces have interdependencies that make parallel work tricky.",
